[?2004l[?2004h> p=Path('README.md'); s=p.read_text(); s+='''
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Delta checkpoints and upgrades
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Each sequence window is applied in sequence order (upserts and tombstones
[?2004l[?2004h> interleaved), together with its cursor in one SQLite transaction. Empty windows
[?2004l[?2004h> still advance the checkpoint. If a page fails, rerunning resumes after the last
[?2004l[?2004h> committed page; an unchanged feed requires only a single empty polling request.
[?2004l[?2004h> Prices are converted with decimal arithmetic, rejecting fractional cents.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Opening a legacy catalog collapses duplicate product rows to the highest
[?2004l[?2004h> `feed_seq` (latest insertion breaks ties) and adds a unique SKU index. Existing
[?2004l[?2004h> product columns and merchandising overrides are preserved. Supplier notices are
[?2004l[?2004h> logged; HTTP 409 notice gates are acknowledged and retried at the same cursor.
[?2004l[?2004h> Notice bodies are not executed as maintenance commands, and sync never prunes
[?2004l[?2004h> local overrides. Expired overrides remain available for historical reports but
[?2004l[?2004h> do not affect today's effective prices.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''; p.write_text(s)
